# Deployment foundation

The generated image runs Phoenix and open-source Oban together as one release,
as required for v1. Database migrations are an explicit release command and are
never run independently by every web boot.

## Required runtime configuration

- `DATABASE_URL`, `PHX_HOST`, `SECRET_KEY_BASE`, and `METRICS_TOKEN`
__IF_AUTH__
- `TOKEN_SIGNING_SECRET`
__END_AUTH__
__IF_GOOGLE__
- `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`, `GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET`, and `GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI`
__IF_HOSTED_DOMAIN__
- `GOOGLE_HOSTED_DOMAIN`
__END_HOSTED_DOMAIN__
__END_GOOGLE__
- Optional email: `RESEND_API_KEY`, `RESEND_WEBHOOK_SECRET`, and `EMAIL_FROM`
- Optional error reporting: `SENTRY_DSN`

Generate independent random values for every secret. The release refuses blank,
placeholder, or clearly weak required values. Keep `/metrics` behind provider
network controls as well as its constant-time bearer-token check.

The liveness probe is `/healthz`; the database-and-migration readiness probe is
`/readyz`. Provider availability and queue delay intentionally do not eject an
otherwise healthy web process.

External Google, Resend, Sentry, Render, and Fly behavior must be checked in a
credentialed staging environment. Local checks validate configuration,
signatures, release startup, migrations, manifests, and fail-closed behavior;
they cannot prove provider acceptance, inbox delivery, OAuth consent, or a real
platform rollout.
